\begin{align*}
\frac{(a+b)^2+(b-c)^2+(c-a)^2}{b^2} &= \frac{a^2 + 2ab + b^2 + b^2 - 2bc + c^2 + c^2 - 2ac + a^2}{b^2} \\
&= \frac{2a^2 + 2b^2 + 2c^2 + 2ab - 2bc - 2ac}{b^2}.
\end{align*}

Next, we factor out a $2$ from the numerator:

\begin{align*}
\frac{2a^2 + 2b^2 + 2c^2 + 2ab - 2bc - 2ac}{b^2} &= \frac{2(a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + ab - bc - ac)}{b^2}.
